    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0514" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/12–1451: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        United States Representative at the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Austin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-22T14:06:00-05:00">December 22,
                            1951—2:06 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Gadel 542. For Roosevelt and Cohen from the
                    Secretary. Re Delga 665, see Gadel 541, general conclusion of which the Pres
                    and I approved <pb facs="0515" n="493" xml:id="pg493"/> after taking into
                    consideration views which you expressed. It seemed to Pres that this shld be
                    handled by the reps of the NATO countries to
                    the GA. Pres felt Mrs. Roosevelt was the ideal
                    person to handle it for US.</p>
                <p>We will inform Mrs. Roosevelt here if she has left Paris.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
